    "title": "Inter Milan Agree to Sign Tarik Muharemovic as Bastoni Nears Barcelona Move - Milan Today",
    "text": "Got story updates? Submit your updates here. ›As two European giants negotiate the transfer of a star defender, the high-stakes clash between Inter Milan and Barcelona is captured in a fractured, cubist-inspired illustration.Milan TodayInter Milan have reportedly reached an agreement to sign 23-year-old Bosnian center-back Tarik Muharemovic from Sassuolo, a move that could pave the way for the departure of star defender Alessandro Bastoni to Barcelona. Bastoni, who joined Inter in 2017 for €31 million, has been heavily linked with a €70 million transfer to the Spanish giants as he looks to take the next step in his career. Why it matters Bastoni's potential exit would be a significant loss for Inter, as he has established himself as one of the team's best players over the past several seasons. However, the Italian club appears willing to cash in on the defender, likely to reinvest the funds into strengthening other areas of the squad. Barcelona, meanwhile, view Bastoni as a key target to bolster their defense under manager Hansi Flick. The details According to reports, Inter have reached an agreement to sign 23-year-old Bosnian center-back Tarik Muharemovic from Sassuolo as a potential replacement for Bastoni. The deal has not been finalized yet, and Inter are also keeping other options like Oumar Solet, Joel Ordóñez, Mario Gila, and Giovanni Leoni on their list of priorities. The move suggests Inter could be open to selling Bastoni to Barcelona for a fee around €70 million, significantly higher than the previously speculated €50 million. Throughout the 2025–26 season, Alessandro Bastoni's future has been a topic of controversy.Inter Milan and Alessandro Bastoni have decided to put any talks regarding his potential transfer on hold until they mathematically secure the Serie A title.Once that objective is achieved, Bastoni is expected to push for a move to Barcelona. The players Alessandro BastoniA 24-year-old Italian defender who has been a key player for Inter Milan since joining the club in 2017 for €31 million. He is now seeking a move to Barcelona, where he is viewed as a key target to bolster their defense.Tarik MuharemovicA 23-year-old Bosnian center-back who currently plays for Sassuolo in Serie A. Inter Milan have reportedly reached an agreement to sign him as a potential replacement for Bastoni.Hansi FlickThe current manager of Barcelona, who is keen to secure Bastoni's signing to strengthen his team's defense. Got photos? Submit your photos here. › What’s next Once Inter Milan mathematically secure the Serie A title, Bastoni is expected to push for a move to Barcelona, with the two clubs having reportedly agreed on a €70 million transfer fee. The takeaway This potential transfer saga highlights the challenges faced by top European clubs in retaining their star players, as Barcelona's interest and Bastoni's desire for a new challenge could lead to a significant departure from Inter Milan. The Italian club's move to sign Muharemovic suggests they are preparing for life after Bastoni, while Barcelona hope to secure a key defensive reinforcement to bolster their squad under Hansi Flick.",
